  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Multiday stretch of dry and tranquil weather \nthis week\n\nStratocumulus clouds will persist today, especially west of I-99\nand north of I-80, but lake effect rain and snow showers have\nended. Clouds will gradually decrease tonight across much of the\nregion and some valley fog is likely across Central PA by\nTuesday morning. By Tuesday afternoon, cloud-free skies will\nabound as high pressure builds in. A splendid week of weather \nis in store.\n\nA string of sunny and increasingly warmer days followed by\nmainly clear and chilly nights is ahead for the remainder of \nthe week into the weekend. Fcst Max temps peak 10-20 degrees \nabove the historical average Fri-Sun while nights will run \ncloser to climo resulting in large diurnal ranges indicative of \na prolonged late Autumn dry spell. Expect ideal conditions for \noutdoor pre-winter activities: raking leaves, set up holiday \ndecorations, or enjoying time outside, it will be an very \npleasant stretch of weather for mid-November. \n\nWith the resumption of another prolonged dry stretch, fire \nweather concerns could increase as we get later into November \nand December. Any particularly windy patterns with minimal \nprecipitation could lead to an elevated risk of rapid wildfire \nspread.",
